{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/kind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/kind"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO"}],"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV4kindAA23MXLStartStopDiscontinueOvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"kind"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this ending starts, stops, or discontinues, determining which barline it is associated with and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether a downward jog is drawn."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLEnding","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLEnding","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","title":"MXLEnding"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopDiscontinue":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The start-stop-discontinue type is used to specify ending types. Typically, the start type is associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a downward"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is typical for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second endings that do not conclude a piece."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue","title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/kind":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this ending starts, stops, or discontinues, determining which barline it is associated with and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether a downward jog is drawn."}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/kind","title":"kind","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}